---
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

interface Props {
  h1: string;
}

const { h1 } = Astro.props;
---
  <h1>{h1}</h1>

<h2 id="resumen">Summary <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Website to advertise a transport company
</p>

<p>
  <strong>GitHub repository <i class="fab fa-github"></i>:</strong>
  <a href="https://github.com/Franco2900/Practica-3---Empresa-de-transporte" target="_blank">Practice 3</a>
</p>

<h2 id="tecnologias">Technologies used <i class="bi bi-laptop"></i> </h2>

<div class="row">

  <div class="col-4">
    Backend: <br>
    NodeJS <i class="fab fa-node-js"></i> with the Express framework 
  </div>

  <div class="col-4">
    Database: <br>
    None
  </div>
  
  <div class="col-4">
    Frontend: <br>
    Bootstrap <i class="fab fa-bootstrap"></i> – Font Awesome <i class="fab fa-font-awesome"></i> – Flag Icons <i class="fi fi-ar"></i> – EJS
  </div>
  
</div>
<br>

<h2 id="descripcion">Full project description <i class="fas fa-align-left"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Until now, all my practice projects were about the backend, giving little importance to the frontend. I only
  used it to show the program running and that was it. That is why this time I decided to focus
  more on the frontend than on the backend.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;I focused on CSS styling and responsive design so it looks right on phones.
  I also built a few image features; for example, some images have options
  that let you view them better, either through a zoom, an overlay or by opening the 
  image directly in a new tab.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Besides good design, I took the opportunity to learn new topics such as cookies
  and locale files, which let me add options to change the language the text is shown in. I also 
  learned how to send emails automatically, so a user can fill out a form on the website 
  and the email arrives at the desired address.
  <br />
</p>


